  "note": "rev 2 = rev 1 plus preset-suite.md §10.3's tropic family (vol-steel, vol-steel-short, vol-steel-roll, vol-skank, vol-bubble, vol-rim, arp-steel-ping, pit-steel-attack, dut-steel; steel-lead, steel-comp, steel-roll, skank, bubble, rim), APPENDED — every rev-1 entry keeps its name, its values and its index, so songs 01-12 are untouched and the drift check still pins them. ONE DEVIATION FROM §10.3's TABLE, forced by the verify-in-preview pass §10.1 asks for: arp-steel-ping is [12,0,7,0,0,0,0,0] loop 7, not [0,12,0,12,0,7,0,0] loop 7. Measured through renderSong at 48 kHz, the written form puts the OCTAVE on tick 1, which is vol-steel's 15 — the loudest instant of the note sounded an octave above the written pitch (+1246 cents) and 42% of the attack's amplitude-weighted energy sat off the fundamental, so the ping read as a grace note rather than as timbre. Re-phasing puts the octave on tick 0 (vol 10, the soft front), the fundamental on the vol-15 peak and the fifth on one 16.7 ms tick: off-fundamental energy 28%, pitch at the peak +23 cents. Same length, same loop index, same two tuned partials [S6] — only the phase moves. preset-suite.md §3 — the album bank, frozen. NOT a playable Song: it holds only sequences, instruments and samples, and its sequences carry a `name` the song format does not have. Songs embed only the entries they use, densely renumbered, NAMES PRESERVED — tests/unit/presets.test.ts resolves every canonical instrument name in every album song back to these values and fails on any drift. Copy from here; do not retype.",
